<section class="gta-box"><h3>Actual route delivery</h3><p class="gta-note">Delivery uses the latest consolidated routing report. It updates after construction completes and routes recalculate.</p><p data-gta-delivery-summary></p><div class="gta-kv"><span>Demand fulfilled · all routes</span><b data-gta-delivery>—</b></div><div class="gta-kv"><span>Demand still unmet</span><b data-gta-missing>—</b></div><div class="gta-kv"><span>Requested transport load</span><b data-gta-requested>—</b></div><div class="gta-kv"><span>Delivered transport load</span><b data-gta-delivered-load>—</b></div><div class="gta-kv"><span>Unmet transport load</span><b data-gta-unmet-load>—</b></div><h3 class="gta-land-title">National land capacity</h3><p data-gta-coverage></p>
<div class="gta-kv"><span>Current land transport load</span><b data-gta-load>—</b></div><div class="gta-kv"><span>Current land capacity</span><b data-gta-capacity>—</b></div><div class="gta-kv"><span>Queued additional capacity</span><b data-gta-pending>—</b></div><div class="gta-kv"><span>Land capacity target</span><b data-gta-target-capacity>—</b></div><div class="gta-kv"><span>Land utilization</span><b data-gta-utilization>—</b></div>
<p class="gta-note">These capacity figures cover your national land network, not every trade route. Queued land capacity counts toward the target while construction finishes.</p><p data-gta-status role="status" aria-live="polite"></p></section>
<section class="gta-box gta-wide"><h3>Why demand is still unmet</h3><p class="gta-note">Bottlenecks may overlap along a route, so their unmet demand is not a total. Your land network, pipelines, and ports share one construction budget.</p><div class="gta-table-wrap" data-gta-blockers></div></section>
